  grid: (2W+1) x H where W=8-12, H=8-12 [observed W=10, H=10]
  background: black (0), dominant color
  separator:
    solid vertical column at center (col W), uniform non-bg color not used elsewhere
    color: gray (5) [observed]; any non-bg color valid per solver
  panels: left (cols 0..W-1) and right (cols W+1..2W) are same size
  foreground_colors: 2-3 distinct colors per panel, never red(2) or blue(1)
  pixels_per_color: 2-4 isolated pixels (no orthogonal fg adjacency)
  total_fg_per_panel: 7-10 [observed]
  panel_relationship:
    both panels have identical fg pixel count
    most pixels are shared (same color at same position in both panels)
    1-2 colors are shifted -- each has exactly 1 pixel in a different position between panels
    shifted positions are always bg in the other panel (no collision)
    at least 1 color is fully shared (anchor)
  output:
    same size as one panel (W x H)
    shared pixels keep their original color
    left-only fg pixels become red (2)
    right-only fg pixels become blue (1)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick panel dims W, H. Choose bg=0, sep_color from non-reserved set (not 0,1,2).
    2. Build the OUTPUT panel first -- place 2-3 fg colors (not 1 or 2) as isolated pixels.
